Defense Against DNS Hijacking
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Implement DNS Security Extensions (DNSSEC) to protect against DNS spoofing
Develop Python scripts to monitor DNS records and detect unauthorized changes
Deploy Zeek network security monitor for DNS traffic analysis
Configure Elasticsearch and Kibana for DNS monitoring visualization
Identify DNS hijacking indicators through traffic pattern analysis
Prerequisites
Basic understanding of DNS protocol and record types
Familiarity with Linux command line operations
Basic Python programming knowledge
Understanding of network security fundamentals
Experience with JSON/YAML configuration files
